<title>MEXICO: POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen rising to 19.36 pct.</title>
<headline>POLL - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen rising to 19.36 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 99 basis points to 19.36 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.37	    19.36		   99 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     18.95	    19.78		   83 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    20.40	    20.83		   43 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     20.24	    20.69		   45 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local time/2330 GMT.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
